      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would also allow business creatives to publish the worlds themselves and sell them to the clients. In case something breaks, the ownership could be transferred, the world fixed, and the ownership then gets transferred back without sending big files. That would be newcomer-friendly as the owner wouldn't have to know how Unity works to get his own world.\n\nIt would also be beneficial to not only transfer ownership but share ownership to make updates on bigger projects possible. Say, My team builds a map, Sam publishes and goes on a holiday trip but it turns out there is a major bug or aspect we have to fix. The team would have to wait for Sam to return to submit changes. A shared world would allow multiple people to do that while he is away.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
